WEBVTT

1
00:00:08.510 --> 00:00:13.050
A control is a safeguard or countermeasure designed to preserve confidentiality,

2
00:00:13.060 --> 00:00:15.369
integrity and availability of data.

3
00:00:15.949 --> 00:00:18.350
We also discussed defense in depth as

4
00:00:18.360 --> 00:00:21.659
an implementation of multiple technical controls.

5
00:00:21.670 --> 00:00:25.979
Now we will look at a scenario that uses multiple controls across the spectrum

6
00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:30.000
including physical technical and administrative controls.

7
00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:36.090
Payroll is one area in nearly every organization that requires

8
00:00:36.099 --> 00:00:39.630
multiple levels of controls to ensure money is not mishandled.

9
00:00:39.970 --> 00:00:43.340
Most will agree that just a single control is too risky.

10
00:00:43.459 --> 00:00:45.919
So multiple controls are often implemented

11
00:00:46.849 --> 00:00:49.669
to prevent payroll personnel from creating a fictional

12
00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:52.490
employee and processing a check for that employee.

13
00:00:52.770 --> 00:00:56.459
A logical or technical control is to ensure that a person

14
00:00:56.470 --> 00:01:00.750
who processes payroll is not able to create a new employee record

15
00:01:00.970 --> 00:01:03.150
and process the check, print file,

16
00:01:03.540 --> 00:01:06.739
a physical control that helps reinforce that technical

17
00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:09.139
control is to ensure the actual paper,

18
00:01:09.150 --> 00:01:11.839
media that checks are printed on is secured in a

19
00:01:11.849 --> 00:01:15.540
place that is not accessible to the person processing payroll.

20
00:01:15.550 --> 00:01:17.660
Both of these controls can further be

21
00:01:17.669 --> 00:01:21.260
enforced by creating an administrative control or policy

22
00:01:21.459 --> 00:01:23.620
that regularly audits the technical and

23
00:01:23.629 --> 00:01:26.779
physical controls by reviewing new employees added

24
00:01:26.790 --> 00:01:31.180
to the system and by logging and verifying the number on physical checks.

25
00:01:32.069 --> 00:01:34.519
Small and medium businesses have a particular

26
00:01:34.529 --> 00:01:37.480
challenge when it comes to technical controls as

27
00:01:37.489 --> 00:01:39.849
they often do not have sufficient personnel to

28
00:01:39.860 --> 00:01:42.069
separate the duties within the payroll system.

29
00:01:42.629 --> 00:01:43.569
In this case,

30
00:01:43.580 --> 00:01:46.629
it may become necessary to implement only physical and

31
00:01:46.639 --> 00:01:49.330
logical controls that align with the business needs.